# Smoke-stability sprint — operator-driven verification artefacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# ``tools/lidar_telemetry_probe.py`` writes no artefacts of its own;
# these patterns cover the byproducts of preflight / pillar / WS-probe
# runs invoked via the operator runbook so they never end up in commits.
preflight_report*.json
pillar_report*.json
lidar_ws_capture*.jsonl
dashboard_capture*.jsonl

# SMOKE_REPORT_*.md other than the canonical one at repo root are
# operator-run-specific (date-stamped) and should not be committed —
# the template at docs/planning/SMOKE_REPORT_TEMPLATE.md is the source
# of truth, and the canonical SMOKE_REPORT.md is kept tracked.
SMOKE_REPORT_*.md
!SMOKE_REPORT.md
!docs/planning/SMOKE_REPORT_TEMPLATE.md
mcp_transcripts/

# Operator-personal dashboard dev overlay (see config/dev_dashboard.yaml.example)
dev_dashboard.yaml

# Workstation smoke artefacts (PR #104 workstation-runbook outputs)
torch-baseline-*.txt
workstation-smoke-*.log
coverage-pr104-*.json

# Windows shell quirk: PowerShell/Git-Bash mis-quoting sometimes creates a
# literal '%SystemDrive%' directory in the worktree root when env-var
# substitution fails. Ignore it so it never lands in a commit.
%SystemDrive%/

# Workstation snapshot inspection artefacts (verify_sensors.py --save-frame)
mock-smoke*.jpg
snap-*.jpg

# Editor-local launch artefacts not intended for the repo
.vscode/launch.local.json

# Config-edit backup files (sed -i.bak / cp foo.yaml foo.yaml.bak.<timestamp>).
# Operators editing /etc/mousedroid/*.yaml on the Jetson — and the smoke runbook
# itself — emit timestamped .bak.* sidecars; these are local-only sidecars and
# must never make it into a commit. Keep this generic so it also catches
# *.bak.YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS_<label> patterns from rover-swap / baud-change drills.
*.bak
*.bak.*

# Web-research scratch fetches (firecrawl/curl output cached under /tmp/ during
# external-doc lookups — see the Wave Rover platform reference memory).
/tmp/wave_rover_*
/tmp/*.html

# config-compat gate worktree scratch. scripts/check_config_compat.py materialises
# the deployed-image SHA into a temporary git worktree via tempfile.mkdtemp
# (prefix "config-compat-"). It normally lands under the system TMPDIR (/tmp,
# %TEMP%), but guard the repo root in case TMPDIR resolves repo-relative on a
# CI/dev host so a stray detached worktree never gets staged.
config-compat-*/
